# flash control plane (operator-side). copy to .env and fill in.
# provider credentials live only here; clients never see them and authenticate
# with their api key.
#
# Everything under "required" is checked by `flash/providers/core/preflight.py` at
# startup; `flash-server` refuses to serve if any of them is missing. Settings
# that only DEGRADE the plane (no GITHUB_TOKEN)
# warn at startup instead of blocking it.
#
# self-hosting? read the self-hosting guide first - the short version is the two lines
# below, and it is a much smaller list than this file suggests:
#
#   FLASH_STANDALONE=1
#   FREESOLO_INTERNAL_KEY=$(openssl rand -hex 32)
#
# IMPORTANT: `flash-server` does NOT read this file. It reads the process
# environment, so copying it to .env is not by itself enough — load it:
#
#   set -a && . ./.env && set +a && flash-server     # shell
#   docker run --env-file .env ...                   # docker

# --- required: Modal GPU substrate ---
MODAL_TOKEN_ID=
MODAL_TOKEN_SECRET=
MODAL_ENVIRONMENT=main
# set to 1 to bypass the shared base-model weight cache.
FLASH_WEIGHT_CACHE_DISABLED=0

# --- required: Flash-owned artifacts (private Azure Blob Storage) ---
FLASH_ARTIFACT_BLOB_ACCOUNT_URL=https://youraccount.blob.core.windows.net
FLASH_ARTIFACT_BLOB_CONTAINER=artifacts
# DefaultAzureCredential is used on the controller. Alternatively supply an account
# connection string here. Account keys never reach training workers: the controller
# issues a container SAS with read/create/write/list permissions and a 27-hour lifetime.
# FLASH_ARTIFACT_BLOB_CONNECTION_STRING=
# A preissued container SAS URL is also accepted (use a read-only one on serving engines).
# FLASH_ARTIFACT_BLOB_SAS_URL=
# Logical namespace inside the private container; independent of any upstream account.
FLASH_ARTIFACT_NAMESPACE=Freesolo-Co

# --- optional: upstream gated base-model downloads and explicit Hub exports ---
HF_TOKEN=

# --- required: control-plane auth ---
# The plane's own auth key. On a self-hosted (FLASH_STANDALONE=1) deployment this is
# the ONLY credential the plane accepts and is therefore the entire trust boundary -
# generate a high-entropy value and treat it like a root password:
#
#   export FREESOLO_INTERNAL_KEY=$(openssl rand -hex 32)
#
# On a managed deployment it is the shared internal key that maps to a single service
# identity without a network call, alongside per-user keys verified against
# {FREESOLO_BASE_URL}/api/auth/verify.
FREESOLO_INTERNAL_KEY=

# --- optional: self-hosting ---
# Run without a Freesolo backend. Off by default. With it set, the plane stops calling
# out for project/environment/billing validation and trusts FREESOLO_INTERNAL_KEY as a
# single-tenant operator credential; external bearer tokens are REJECTED rather than
# accepted unverified. Single tenant: all authenticated clients share the same resources.
# FLASH_STANDALONE=1

# --- optional: deployment topology ---
# Where Flash keeps its local state: the saved login, the SQLite database, run records, and
# results. Defaults to ~/.flash (= /root/.flash for the container's default user, which is the
# path the Dockerfile declares as a VOLUME). Set this for a rootless container, a Kubernetes
# PVC, a read-only home directory, or a systemd unit with ProtectHome. Everything moves
# together, so point it at ONE durable location and mount a volume there.
# FLASH_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/flash
# Log verbosity for `flash-server`: DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR, CRITICAL. The server defaults
# to INFO -- provider resolution, capability removal, reaper startup, and degraded-config
# warnings are all reported at INFO/WARNING. An unrecognized value falls back to the default
# rather than blocking startup.
# FLASH_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# `text` (default) or `json`. JSON emits one object per line for a structured log sink. The
# same information is logged either way; only the punctuation differs.
# FLASH_LOG_FORMAT=text
# Bind address for `flash-server`. Defaults to 127.0.0.1; the container image passes 0.0.0.0
# explicitly. The --host and --port flags win over both of these.
# FLASH_SERVER_HOST=127.0.0.1
# Port for `flash-server`, default 8080. Must be 1-65535: an unusable value stops startup
# rather than silently binding the default, since a plane listening on the wrong port looks
# healthy and is unreachable.
# FLASH_SERVER_PORT=8080
# How long (seconds) to wait for a SQLite lock held by another writer, default 30. Raise it on
# networked storage, where a lock can be held far longer than on a local volume. This changes
# only patience: journal mode, synchronous, and foreign keys are correctness settings and are
# deliberately not configurable.
# FLASH_SQLITE_BUSY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=30

# --- optional ---
# Server token for the environment repository. Without it, environments hosted in a
# private GitHub repo cannot be fetched; environments in public GitHub repos still work,
# so this warns at startup rather than blocking it. (A local directory is never a valid
# environment source - the GPU worker fetches the environment itself.)
GITHUB_TOKEN=
# Where to verify user keys. Defaults to https://api.freesolo.co when unset. Ignored
# under FLASH_STANDALONE=1, which verifies nothing over the network.
# FREESOLO_BASE_URL=
# Adapter serving is delegated to a multi-LoRA serving app (a Modal app that serves
# every adapter on one GPU per base model, scaling to zero when idle).
# `flash deploy`/`undeploy`/`chat` register/deregister/chat against it. Defaults to the
# hosted URL when unset; point it at your own deployment to self-host serving.
#
# Under FLASH_STANDALONE=1 there is NO default: those three commands error out until this
# is set to a backend YOU operate. Every serving request carries FREESOLO_INTERNAL_KEY,
# which on a self-hosted plane is the credential controlling that plane, so pointing it at
# a service you do not run would hand that credential over. Training never uses this.
#
# A Freesolo-hosted value is refused the same way an unset one is -- assigning the hosted
# URL here does not get you past the guard, it just produces the same error. Set it to
# YOUR serving deployment; the managed plane gets the hosted URL from the code default.
# FREESOLO_SERVING_URL=https://serving.example.internal
# The worker container image is not configurable: every provider runs the published
# ghcr.io/freesolo-co/flash-worker tags (per-GPU-arch kernel-cache variants, falling back to the
# base :cu128), selected by GPU class in flash/providers/_lifecycle/net/worker.py.

# Optional Nebius-only Spot training. Install/authenticate the Nebius CLI on the control plane.
# Public config: [gpu] spot = true. Spot is never an implicit Modal fallback.
# Use a USD-billed project. Region must match the project/subnet and host image.
# Host image must include Docker, NVIDIA driver/container toolkit, and outbound internet.
# Worker images are the same curated per-GPU images used by Modal.
FLASH_NEBIUS_PROJECT_ID=
FLASH_NEBIUS_REGION=
FLASH_NEBIUS_SUBNET_ID=
FLASH_NEBIUS_IMAGE_ID=
